# Coverage output directories (istanbul/vitest, and test-genie's per-scenario run
# store -- see test-genie internal/shared/artifacts/paths.go: CoverageRoot).
#
# These patterns are deliberately ANCHORED to project roots. Do NOT collapse them
# back into a bare "coverage" rule: "coverage" is also a real *source* name in this
# repo -- a proto domain under packages/proto/**/v1/coverage/ and Go packages under
# scenarios/data-backup-manager/{api/handlers,api/internal,cli/domains}/coverage/.
# An unanchored rule silently excludes that source from git, which previously left
# data-backup-manager and meta-optimization-manager unbuildable from a fresh clone.
# Coverage *output* always lands at a project root; coverage *source* lives deeper.
# Verify with `git check-ignore -v <path>` before widening these.
/coverage/
packages/*/coverage/
scenarios/*/coverage/
scenarios/*/ui/coverage/
# Test Genie file-determined phase results are runtime cache state, not source.
scenarios/*/phase-cache/
templates/scenarios/*/coverage/
templates/scenarios/*/ui/coverage/
*.lcov
**/coverage*.html
**/coverage*_report.*
**/coverage-report.*
**/TEST_COVERAGE_REPORT.*
**/coverage-detailed.*
**/coverage*.out
**/test-output*.txt
**/*test-output*.txt
**/test.bin
**/test-build
**/api/*-api
**/api/webconsole
# Ad-hoc Go build output. `go build` with no -o names the binary after its
# containing directory, so a bare `go build .` in api/ or cli/ drops an
# extensionless executable right next to the source. Every compiled binary that
# reached this repo's history arrived this way (never via the standard
# `go build -o "$(SCENARIO_NAME)-api"` above, which **/api/*-api already covers).
# gitignore cannot express "extensionless executable", so these patterns cover
# only the predictable shapes; `vrooli hygiene` owns the general backstop via its
# tracked_binaries check.
scenarios/*/api/api
scenarios/*/api/main
scenarios/*/cli/cli
scenarios/*/cli/main
resources/*/api/api
resources/*/api/main
resources/*/cli/main
# Build-freshness manifests: regenerable, host-specific cache stamped next to
# each build artifact (mtime/toolchain-keyed, self-healing). Never committed.
**/*.freshness.json
bin/
.vrooli/*-agents.json
.vrooli/*.lock
.vrooli/browserless/
.vrooli/running-resources.json
.vrooli/schemas/resource-definitions.json

